\chapter{Executive Summary}

Modern engineering architectures are defined by AI-native system design,
continuous compliance enforcement, Model-Based Systems Engineering (MBSE),
and the elimination of architectural entropy. This implementation package
standardizes the methodology for building resilient, scalable, and secure
systems that balance AI velocity with disciplined engineering governance.

\chapter{Pillars of Modern Engineering Architecture}

\section{AI-Native First Design}

\begin{itemize}
    \item Integration of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) patterns
          and agentic workflows into the core execution path.
    \item Deployment of Domain-Specific Language Models (DSLMs) for
          high-stakes operational environments.
    \item Optimization of token economics and reduction of hallucination
          through domain-constrained inference.
\end{itemize}

\section{Serverless-First and FinOps Optimization}

\begin{itemize}
    \item Durable functions and managed stateful queues for cost-efficient
          execution.
    \item Pay-per-use compute models aligned with business financial outcomes.
    \item Architectural drift mitigation through automated scaling policies.
\end{itemize}

\section{Decentralized Data Ownership (Data Mesh)}

\begin{itemize}
    \item Data treated as a product owned by domain-specific teams.
    \item Elimination of central pipeline bottlenecks.
    \item Autonomous domain-level governance and schema evolution.
\end{itemize}

\section{Continuous Compliance and Zero Trust Security}

\begin{itemize}
    \item Automated risk identification and verification loops.
    \item Zero Trust Architecture (ZTA) enforced across all layers.
    \item Continuous compliance tracking integrated into the engineering lifecycle.
\end{itemize}

